(a) 1970 and 1971-Nil. (i) to (iii) N/A. 1972, 1.
(i)	M.B., B.S. London, M.R.C.S., L.R.C.P, D.P.M., England, M.R.C. Psychiatry; (ii) House Physician, Charing Cross Hospital, Royal Air Force as Medical Officer, 16 years in general medicine and forensic psychiatry, Honorary Senior Lecturer (Psychiatry), The London Hospital Medical College; (iii) Salary Range-1972, $26,800-$35,000; 1973, $28,700-$37,500; 1974, $32,000-$41,600; 1975, $34,500- $44,900. 1973, 2. Case 1, See 1972, Case 2 (i) BSC, MD, CM, University of Montreal, Fellowship of Psychiatry and Surgeon, Canada Certificate in Psychiatry, Royal Surgeon;
(ii)	Canadian Army Medical Corps Psychiatrist in 1941 Served Post Work regular Army Practice of Psychiatry in Kingston, Ontario Consultant to Department of Veteran Affairs at Queen's University Medical School 1960 appointed as Psychiatrist for CPS on part-time basis; (iii) Salary range 1973, $28,700-$37,500; 1974, $32,000-$41,600; 1975, $34,500-$44,900. 1974, 4. Case 1, See 1972; Case 2, See 1973; Case 3, (i) MD, LMCC, College of Physicians and Surgeons of Ontario, C.R.C.P. (C), F.R.C.P. (C), Diploma in Psychiatry, (ii) Staff Physician-Ontario Hospital, London, Staff Physician-Toronto Psychiatric Hospital, Staff Physician-Toronto Western Hospital; (iii) Salary range 1974, $29,300-$38,700, 1975, $31,700-$41,700, Case, 4. (i) Internship at Aberdeen Royal Infirmary, (ii) Medical Officer, RAF 1953 transferred to RCAF as Staff Medical Officer Internal Medicine at Toronto Military Hospital Staff Officer Medical Services at Maritime Air Command France as Senior Medical Officer in No. 1 Air Division in Europe Armed Forces Hospital, Kingston, Surgeon and Psychiatrist; (iii) Salary range 1974, $29,300-$38,700; 1975, $31,700-$41,700. 1975, 4. Case 1; See 1972; Case 2; See 1973; Case 3 and 4: See 1974. (b) Nil for 1970 to 1975 inclusive.
